# PRs and git

- Branch per task. Small PRs, one intent, under ~400 changed lines when possible. Cursor cloud agents use the `cursor/` branch prefix their runner requires.
- Conventional titles: `feat|fix|test|docs|refactor|chore|perf(scope): summary`.
- PR body sections (required): What · Why · How verified (exact commands + trimmed output) · Numbers changed (before → after + command) · Risks · Not done / follow-ups · Plan link (`.cursor/plans/...`) · Agent run link if any.
- Run `.cursor/skills/verify-receipts/SKILL.md` before opening a PR that touches numbers, tests, or scorers.
- Attach artifacts for anything visual or behavioral (screenshot, short video, eval table).
- Never force-push shared branches, rewrite history, tag, or publish. A human merges. The shell guard blocks `git pull --rebase` because the deny rule matches `rebase`.
- Address every Bugbot finding: fix it or reply with a reason. Don't silently resolve.
